# The Network: Apple China
#
# Expects Domestic, referenced with extended-matching. Must precede Platforms/Apple.list, whose apple.com suffix would otherwise take the -cn location and Maps hosts. Those hosts carry the region inside a label (gspe19-cn-ssl, gsp10-ssl-cn), which a suffix rule cannot see, so the wildcard does that work.
#
# The mainland-operated estate: iCloud on GCBD, the .cn store, and the location, Maps and search endpoints that serve mainland devices. Through a proxy exit they still answer, which is how the mismatch hides; measured as mainland iCloud IMAP riding the proxy while classified under the old services list.

DOMAIN-SUFFIX,apple.com.cn
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,icloud.com.cn
DOMAIN-WILDCARD,gsp*-cn*.ls.apple.com
DOMAIN,api.smoot.apple.cn
DOMAIN,cl2-cn.apple.com
DOMAIN,cl4-cn.apple.com
DOMAIN,gs-loc-cn.apple.com
